# LoreKeeper Ask — pinning a gold standard / example

When the owner pins a gold Ask answer (baseline, never-worse, “lock this sample”):

## Do

1. **Raise the floor** — newer owner-approved “even better” samples replace thinner golds when they say so.
2. **Keep prior good beats** — if an earlier gold (or owner-checked answer) already had a must-keep beat and the notes still support it, the new gold and the next fix **must not drop it**. Especially: **entry-reason**, **can’t-leave-yet**, **antagonist softer side / not without a soul**, **antagonist stakes about her** (asset vs threat / how he would see her), named antagonist sparse facts, origin before the adventure.
3. **Voice vs checklist** — “never worse” means both: (a) planning-brief voice/density stays at least as strong, and (b) previously good completeness slots stay covered when sources still have them.
4. **Invent nothing** — if transport mechanics (or any beat) are unwritten, omit them; still restate saved *reason* and *can’t leave yet* when those exist.

## Do not

- Treat gold as voice-only and let Sonnet “upgrade” by dropping entry-reason or other already-good slots
- Soften machine locks so a thinner answer still passes
- Mix who-is / leave-off / writing-next golds into an unrelated pass

